@startuml
' Phase 10b — Surface: planned infrastructure.
' Copy to summary.uml at part end and edit to the as-built state.

title Phase 10b — Surface (planned)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-console (Go; imports contracts only)" as console {
  component "client + commands + approvals + config (from 10a)" as core
  component "shared view-model layer (surface-agnostic)" as vm
  component "Surface interface" as surface
  component "surface registry + selection" as registry
  component "surface conformance test-kit" as kit
  component "tui (terminal implements Surface; from 10a)" as tui
}

package "future UI / TUI / GUI (PR #17 placeholder)" as future {
  component "web surface (implements Surface)" as web
  component "desktop surface (Wails; implements Surface)" as desktop
}

package "aa-contracts (v1 schemas + openapi control plane)" as contracts
component "control plane (phase 10 core: loopback HTTP/JSON, bearer)" as server

contracts --> core
core --> vm
vm --> surface
surface --> registry
surface --> tui
tui --> core : intents / decisions
kit ..> surface : validates any surface
surface ..> web : future implementation (PR #17)
surface ..> desktop : future implementation (PR #17)
core ..> server : HTTP/JSON (loopback, bearer)

note right of vm
  ADR-P10B-002: one shared view-model
  layer renders to every surface;
  surfaces are views, not logic.
end note

note bottom of surface
  ADR-P10B-001/003: surfaces are
  pluggable behind one Surface
  interface and a conformance
  contract, so a new surface is
  correct by construction. No surface
  may reach the control plane directly.
end note

note bottom of registry
  ADR-P10B-004: surface selection is
  explicit and deterministic; the
  chosen surface is configuration,
  reproducible in tests.
end note

note bottom of tui
  ADR-P10B-005: the terminal from part
  10a is refactored onto the shared
  layer with no behavior change.
end note

@enduml
